Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Private Outside MGH Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MARCELYN CAROL MOLLOY  M D  HELENANNE D ALESSANDRO  M D  BETHANY L  NIELL  M D  Resident  Hong Xiao  M D  Signed Out by  Elena F Brachtel  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  49 year old female with left lower inner breast calcifications    benign versus other  targeted calcifications are in specimen  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY  CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH MIXED LOBULAR AND DUCTAL FEATURES  FOCAL COMEDONECROSIS AND CALCIFICATIONS   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The carcinoma in situ is of solid type with intermediate nuclear grade  extensively involving ducts and lobules in all cores and spanning at least 0 8cm in this limited sample  The carcinoma in situ tumor cells are mostly negative for E cadherin by immunohistochemistry  which would favor a lobular subtype  However  there is patchy E cadherin positivity in some ducts  in conjunction with the presence of focal comedonecrosis  the diagnosis of carcinoma in situ with mixed lobular and ductal features is favored  Definitive microinvasion could not be demonstrated by immunohistochemistry for p63  calponin  myosin and cytokeratin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen and progesterone receptor proteins will be reported in an addendum  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN    left breast   are 7 cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm which are submitted in toto as cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Also received in the same container is a blue casset